## Overview

`service-health` provides a configurable `HealthService`, documented Effect schemas, a `HealthApiGroup`, and an exported handler implementation. It exposes `/health`, `/health/live`, `/health/ready`, and `/health/started`. Successful checks return `UP`; any failed check produces `DOWN`, and the HTTP contract maps unhealthy responses to status 503. Package consumers import the complete public API from `@krak-stack/registry/service-health`.

## Included Files

- `services/health/index.ts` - public barrel and health service
- `services/health/schema.ts` - health response schemas and HTTP status metadata
- `services/health/api.group.ts` - public health API group
- `services/health/api.builder.ts` - reusable handler implementation

## Register The API Group

Add `HealthApiGroup` after applying authentication middleware to application groups so health endpoints remain public. Apply the root prefix after adding the health group so every endpoint receives the same prefix.

```ts
import { HealthApiGroup } from "@/services/health";

export const Api = HttpApi.make("AppApi")
  .add(ApplicationApiGroup)
  .middleware(AuthMiddleware)
  .add(HealthApiGroup)
  .prefix("/api");
```

## Build And Register The Handler

Bind the exported `healthHandler` implementation to the parent API group. Configure checks with `HealthService.layerWith`, then provide the resulting layer to the application's `HttpApiBuilder` layer. The handler automatically uses the paths and prefix already present on `Api`. Check dependencies such as `DB` are captured when the health service layer is built.

```ts
import { Effect, Layer } from "effect";
import { HttpApiBuilder } from "effect/unstable/httpapi";

import { Api } from "@/api";
import { DB } from "@/services/database";
import { healthHandler, HealthService } from "@/services/health";

const healthLayer = HttpApiBuilder.group(Api, "health", healthHandler).pipe(
  Layer.provide(
    HealthService.layerWith({
      checks: {
        ready: [
          {
            name: "database",
            check: Effect.gen(function* () {
              const db = yield* DB;
              yield* db.$client`SELECT 1`;
              return HealthService.up();
            }).pipe(Effect.timeout("2 seconds")),
          },
        ],
      },
    }),
  ),
);

export const apiLayer = HttpApiBuilder.layer(Api).pipe(
  Layer.provide(healthLayer),
  Layer.provide(DB.layer),
);
```

Failed effects, defects, and timeouts become `DOWN` results without exposing internal errors. Optional diagnostic data accepts non-sensitive string, number, and boolean values.
